## The page's plate.  The report's `theme` option (dark | light | auto,
## default dark) is read by weewx-skyfield's SkyPage straight out of THIS
## report's skin dict -- celestial_sky hands it over -- so the option is
## spelled and valued exactly as skyfield's own Sky page spells it, and
## `auto` (light while the sun is up at generation time) is skyfield's
## sunrise logic, not a second copy of it.  Resolved HERE, at generation:
## the dome and the Next Visible Pass chart arrive as skyfield SVG with
## their colors already inside them and the javascript refetches them
## every 60 s, so a browser-side toggle could not move them and the next
## refetch would undo it anyway.  Dark without a capable $sky_page: the
## light plate is the paper the charts are drawn on, and there are no
## charts on that tier.  Guarded, like every other skyfield call here --
## a page that does not generate is the worse failure (7.2's lesson).
## ONE guarded lookup serves both the class and the charts' palette.
## skyfield RAISES on an unknown theme (SkyPageUsageError passes through
## its panel guard by design), so asking it a second time for the palette
## would put that raise inside the dome's own #try and cost a typo the
## whole dome and pass panel -- the plate is what a typo may cost.
## theme() raises ONLY on a value that is not dark, light or auto, so a
## raise here is a misconfigured report and gets a log line -- otherwise
## a typo is invisible: the page just renders dark for ever.  The
## hasattr guard keeps the older-skyfield case quiet, where there is no
## theme() and no way to know whether anyone asked for one.  This is the
## only site that logs; the fragment templates resolve the same way and
## stay silent, or one typo would print eleven lines a cycle.
#set $theme = 'dark'
#if $sky_page and hasattr($sky_page, 'theme')
#try
#set $theme = str($sky_page.theme($almanac))
#except
#silent logging.getLogger('user.celestial').warning("The Celestial report has an unusable theme option; rendering the dark plate.  Valid values are dark, light and auto.")
#end try
#end if
